## 2. Case Result & Defect Severity Vocabulary (`A9`, `A10`)

Case outcomes and defect severities follow `shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`:

| Case Status | Meaning & Evidence Rule | Defect Severity (when `FAIL`) |
|---|---|---|
| **`PASS`** | All steps executed on `{{revision_notation}}`, expected UI/API outcome and persistence read-back observed, zero console/network regressions | None |
| **`FAIL`** | Observed behavior contradicts expected outcome, persistence read-back fails, or intermittent (flaky) outcome across reruns | Graded **`BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR`** ([03]({{ref_03}})) |
| **`BLOCKED`** | Precondition unmet, target service down, or verification tool (`{{ui_tool}}` / `{{api_tool}}`) and fallback unreachable (`A7`) | Never counts as `PASS` |
| **`NOT_RUN`** | Deferred or out of selected run scope with explicit reason | Never counts as `PASS` |

